# Actual Budget stack secrets (services VM)
# Copy to .sops.env and encrypt with:
#   SOPS_AGE_KEY_FILE=../../sops_age_key.txt sops -e -i .sops.env
#
# Key-set contract: this file, the real .sops.env and the test fixture
# tests/fixtures/actual.sops.env must all carry EXACTLY the same keys — the
# stack-env-drift lint fails on any difference.
#
# Reminder from CLAUDE.md (finding #30): Compose INTERPOLATES env_file
# values, so any value containing '$' must be single-quoted before
# encrypting. `openssl rand -hex` cannot emit one.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The server password, set headlessly by actual_init on the first deploy via
# POST /account/bootstrap. ONE password for the whole server (single-user
# password mode) — it is what every Actual client asks for on connect.
#
# 🚨 FIRST-RUN-ONLY, in one direction: actual_init refuses to run while this
# is empty or still changeme_ (a placeholder password on a finance server in
# a public repo is the trap it guards), but once the server is bootstrapped
# this key is never consulted again — the password's source of truth moves to
# account.sqlite, and changing it later is the client UI or
# `docker exec -it actual node scripts/reset-password.js`, NOT this file.
# Rotating the value here does nothing, silently, by design.
# Generate: openssl rand -base64 24
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
ACTUAL_INIT_PASSWORD=changeme_strong_password

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OIDC (native; ships READY and OFF — see compose.yaml for the enable steps
# and the first-login-becomes-owner warning).
#
# INERT until the two ACTUAL_OPENID_* lines in compose.yaml are uncommented
# AND `node scripts/enable-openid.js` is run: the server reads these into
# config at boot but consults the openId config only once the login method
# in the DATABASE says openid. Filling them in early breaks nothing.
#
# Values come from the Authentik provider for actual.svc.idanreed.com
# (redirect URI https://actual.svc.idanreed.com/openid/callback), which
# needs the production age key to reach headscale-vps/secrets.sops.yaml —
# same posture as vaultwarden/ghostfolio: placeholders until the operator
# lands the secret.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
ACTUAL_OPENID_CLIENT_ID=changeme_authentik_client_id
ACTUAL_OPENID_CLIENT_SECRET=changeme_authentik_client_secret
